<h2 id="when" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">2. Trigger aliases</h2>

| User token | CLI step |
|------------|----------|
| **`pwlad 0`** / **`pv`** / **`preview`** | `0-preview` |
| **`pwlad 1`** / **`continent`** | `1-continent` |
| **`pwlad 2`** … **`6`** / scope name | `2-number` … `6-other` |
| **`pwlad ladder`** / **`full`** | `default-ladder` (0-preview → … → 6-other; stop on first fail) |

**Purge passthrough:** **`--pb`** → chain pre-purge; **`--pa`** → post-success purge (per sub-step on `ladder`). See README_UBS § flags.

**Recover passthrough:** **`--recover`**, **`--auto-recover-enabled`**, **`--recover-pw`**, **`--step-run-id`** (legacy **`--ladder-id`**) — mutually exclusive rules in README § “Recover — which flag when”.

