<h2 id="fail" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Failure / recover</h2>

After a failed step, stderr includes:

- **`STEP_RUN_FAIL_PHASE=chain|playwright`** — which phase failed
- **`[PWLAD_RECOVER_HINT]`** — copy-paste retry commands (also lists `step_run_id` + `chain_id`)
- **`[PWLAD_DIAGNOSE]`** at run start — mode, tries left

| Fail phase | Meaning | First retry (from hint) |
|------------|---------|-------------------------|
| **chain** | Paragraph generation failed / timed out | Same step run + `--recover --step-run-id …` or `--auto-recover-enabled` |
| **playwright** | Chain OK; browser grading failed | Same step run + `--recover --step-run-id …` or `playwright --chain-id … --recover-pw` |

**Agent rule:** Prefer stderr **`[PWLAD_RECOVER_HINT]`** over reconstructing flags. Flag semantics: README_UBS § “Recover — which flag when”.

